{"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles"]]},"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Ensembles"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Getting Started"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SwiftDataIntegration","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SyncLifecycle","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleDelegate"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials"}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ensembles\/gettingstarted"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/GettingStarted","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Set up Ensembles to sync a Core Data or SwiftData persistent store across devices."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ensembles synchronizes SQLite stores by recording local changes as events and exchanging them through a cloud backend. It works with both Core Data and SwiftData."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Using SwiftData?","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" See "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SwiftDataIntegration","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" for a complete guide — you never need to touch Core Data directly."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This guide covers Core Data setup, starting with a complete working example using "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Develop with Claude Code","anchor":"Develop-with-Claude-Code"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you use "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/claude.com\/claude-code","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", install the Ensembles skill first. It teaches Claude the API, the cloud backends, Ensembles 2 → 3 migration, the seed policy, and the common pitfalls, so it writes correct setup code and diagnoses sync issues without hand-holding:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["\/plugin marketplace add mentalfaculty\/Ensembles3","\/plugin install ensembles@ensembles"]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Add Ensembles to Your Project","anchor":"Add-Ensembles-to-Your-Project"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the Ensembles package to your "},{"code":"Package.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or via Xcode’s package dependencies:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["https:\/\/github.com\/mentalfaculty\/Ensembles3.git"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Import the core module and one cloud backend:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import Ensembles","import EnsemblesCloudKit   \/\/ or EnsemblesLocalFile, EnsemblesMemory"]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Complete Example: Core Data with CloudKit","anchor":"Complete-Example-Core-Data-with-CloudKit"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Here’s a complete, working setup for a SwiftUI app that syncs via CloudKit. This uses "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", which creates the Core Data stack for you and syncs automatically."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"1. Create Your Core Data Model","anchor":"1-Create-Your-Core-Data-Model"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In Xcode, add a "},{"code":".xcdatamodeld","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" file to your project (e.g., "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Model.xcdatamodeld","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":"). Define your entities as usual. For this example, we’ll assume a "},{"code":"Note","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" entity with "},{"code":"title","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (String) and "},{"code":"uniqueID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (String) attributes."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"2. Define Your Model with `Syncable`","anchor":"2-Define-Your-Model-with-Syncable"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For deduplication, conform your "},{"code":"NSManagedObject","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" subclass to the "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/Syncable","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol and specify which property holds the global identifier. A UUID assigned at creation time is usually the best choice:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import CoreData","import Ensembles","","class Note: NSManagedObject, Syncable {","    static let globalIdentifierKey = \"uniqueID\"","    @NSManaged var uniqueID: String","    @NSManaged var title: String","}"]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A global identifier ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"must never change"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" once it has been assigned. Changing it after sync has begun will cause duplicates or data loss.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside","style":"important","name":"Important"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use a fixed, meaningful value instead of a UUID for singleton objects or reference data like tags, where two devices might independently create the same logical object."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"3. Set Up the Container","anchor":"3-Set-Up-the-Container"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiftUI","import Ensembles","import EnsemblesCloudKit","","@main","struct MyApp: App {","    let syncContainer: CoreDataEnsembleContainer","","    init() {","        \/\/ The model URL points to the .momd bundle compiled from your .xcdatamodeld","        let modelURL = Bundle.main.url(forResource: \"Model\", withExtension: \"momd\")!","","        \/\/ This creates a full Core Data stack automatically:","        \/\/ - SQLite store at Application Support\/MyNotes.sqlite","        \/\/ - Main-queue viewContext for your UI","        \/\/ - Auto-sync on save, on app activation, and on a 5-minute timer","        let container = CoreDataEnsembleContainer(","            name: \"MyNotes\",","            modelURL: modelURL,","            cloudFileSystem: CloudKitFileSystem(","                privateDatabaseForUbiquityContainerIdentifier: \"iCloud.com.example.mynotes\",","                schemaVersion: .v2","            )","        )!","","        self.syncContainer = container","    }","","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup {","            ContentView()","                .environment(","                    \\.managedObjectContext,","                    syncContainer.viewContext","                )","        }","    }","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"That’s the complete setup. The container discovers "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/Syncable","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" conformances automatically, attaches to the cloud, and begins syncing. Remote changes are merged into "},{"code":"viewContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" so your UI stays up to date."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"4. Respond to Events (Optional)","anchor":"4-Respond-to-Events-Optional"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Called after remote changes are merged into viewContext","container.didSaveMergeChanges = { notification in","    print(\"Merged remote changes\")","}","","\/\/ Called if a sync fails","container.didEncounterError = { error in","    print(\"Sync error: \\(error)\")","}"]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Using a Custom Store Location","anchor":"Using-a-Custom-Store-Location"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you need control over where the SQLite file lives, pass an explicit "},{"code":"storeURL","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let appSupport = FileManager.default.urls(","    for: .applicationSupportDirectory, in: .userDomainMask",").first!","let storeURL = appSupport.appendingPathComponent(\"MyApp\/data.sqlite\")","try FileManager.default.createDirectory(","    at: storeURL.deletingLastPathComponent(),","    withIntermediateDirectories: true",")","","let container = CoreDataEnsembleContainer(","    name: \"MyNotes\",","    storeURL: storeURL,","    modelURL: Bundle.main.url(forResource: \"Model\", withExtension: \"momd\")!,","    cloudFileSystem: CloudKitFileSystem(","        privateDatabaseForUbiquityContainerIdentifier: \"iCloud.com.example.mynotes\",","        schemaVersion: .v2","    )",")!"]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Working with an Existing Core Data Stack","anchor":"Working-with-an-Existing-Core-Data-Stack"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you already have an "},{"code":"NSPersistentContainer","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", pass it in directly:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let container = CoreDataEnsembleContainer(","    persistentContainer: myPersistentContainer,","    cloudFileSystem: cloudFS",")"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Or if you have an existing "},{"code":"NSManagedObjectContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let container = CoreDataEnsembleContainer(","    name: \"MyNotes\",","    viewContext: myContext,","    persistentStoreURL: myStoreURL,","    managedObjectModel: myContext.persistentStoreCoordinator!.managedObjectModel,","    managedObjectModels: nil,","    cloudFileSystem: cloudFS",")"]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Auto-Sync Configuration","anchor":"Auto-Sync-Configuration"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Control when syncing occurs with "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/AutoSyncPolicy","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let config = EnsembleContainerConfiguration(","    autoSyncPolicy: [.onSave, .onTimer],   \/\/ Sync on save and timer, not on activation","    timerInterval: 30                       \/\/ Timer fires every 30 seconds",")","let container = CoreDataEnsembleContainer(","    name: \"MyNotes\",","    modelURL: modelURL,","    cloudFileSystem: cloudFS,","    configuration: config",")"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Set "},{"code":"autoSyncPolicy","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"code":".manual","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and call "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer\/sync()","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" yourself for full control over timing."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Backward Compatibility with Ensembles 2","anchor":"Backward-Compatibility-with-Ensembles-2"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you’re transitioning from Ensembles 2 and some users may still be on E2, set the compatibility mode:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let config = EnsembleContainerConfiguration(","    compatibilityMode: .ensembles2Compatible",")"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This restricts exports to formats that Ensembles 2 peers can parse. Switch to "},{"code":".ensembles3","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (the default) once all users have upgraded."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The Manual Way: CoreDataEnsemble","anchor":"The-Manual-Way-CoreDataEnsemble"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For more control over the sync lifecycle, use "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" directly. This is useful when you need to manage attach\/detach timing, handle specific delegate methods, or integrate with a complex Core Data stack."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Create and Attach","anchor":"Create-and-Attach"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import Ensembles","import EnsemblesCloudKit","","\/\/ Get the store URL from your persistent store coordinator","let store = persistentStoreCoordinator.persistentStores.first!","let storeURL = store.url!","let modelURL = Bundle.main.url(forResource: \"Model\", withExtension: \"momd\")!","","let ensemble = CoreDataEnsemble(","    ensembleIdentifier: \"MyNotes\",","    persistentStoreURL: storeURL,","    managedObjectModelURL: modelURL,","    cloudFileSystem: CloudKitFileSystem(","        privateDatabaseForUbiquityContainerIdentifier: \"iCloud.com.example.mynotes\",","        schemaVersion: .v2","    )",")","ensemble?.delegate = self","","\/\/ Attach registers this device in the cloud","try await ensemble?.attachPersistentStore()"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/ensembleIdentifier","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" must be the same on all devices that should sync together. If you have multiple persistent stores, create one ensemble per store with a unique identifier."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Avoid saving to the persistent store while attaching. If a save is detected, attachment will fail with an error and you will need to retry.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside","style":"important","name":"Important"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Sync Changes","anchor":"Sync-Changes"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Call "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/sync(options:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" periodically — for example, when the app enters the foreground, on a timer, or in response to a push notification:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["try await ensemble?.sync()"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A sync downloads remote events, replays them into the local store, and uploads new local events. Sync errors are usually transient — just retry later."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Handle the Delegate","anchor":"Handle-the-Delegate"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Implement "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleDelegate","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" to respond to sync events. The most important method merges remote changes into your main context:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["extension AppDelegate: CoreDataEnsembleDelegate {","    func coreDataEnsemble(","        _ ensemble: CoreDataEnsemble,","        didSaveMergeChangesWith notification: Notification","    ) {","        viewContext.perform {","            self.viewContext.mergeChanges(fromContextDidSave: notification)","        }","    }","}"]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"With ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/Syncable","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" conformances are discovered automatically and no ","type":"text"},{"code":"globalIdentifiersForManagedObjects","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" implementation is needed. When you use ","type":"text"},{"code":"CoreDataEnsemble","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" directly, the delegate method is required — but if your classes conform to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Syncable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" it is a one-liner:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["func coreDataEnsemble(","    _ ensemble: CoreDataEnsemble,","    globalIdentifiersForManagedObjects objects: [NSManagedObject]",") -> [String] {","    ensemble.syncableGlobalIdentifiers(forManagedObjects: objects)","}"],"type":"codeListing"}],"type":"aside","style":"tip","name":"Tip"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Other delegate methods let you:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Inspect and repair merge data","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" before it’s committed ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"shouldSaveMergedChangesIn:reparationContext:"},{"type":"text","text":")"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Handle save failures","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" during merging ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"didFailToSaveMergedChangesIn:error:reparationContext:"},{"type":"text","text":")"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"React to forced detaches","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" caused by identity changes or data corruption ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"didDetachWithError:"},{"type":"text","text":")"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"See "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/ConflictResolution","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" for more on conflict handling and the reparation context."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Detach","anchor":"Detach"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To stop syncing, detach from the cloud:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["try await ensemble?.detachPersistentStore()"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This removes local sync data (event logs and metadata). The persistent store itself is not affected. You can re-attach later to resume syncing."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Seed Policies","anchor":"Seed-Policies"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SeedPolicy","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" parameter controls how existing data in the store is handled during attachment:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SeedPolicy\/mergeAllData","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (default) — Imports local data so it can be merged with data from other devices."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SeedPolicy\/excludeLocalData","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — Ignores local data. Use this when you want to start fresh from cloud data."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Sync Options","anchor":"Sync-Options"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For advanced control, pass "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SyncOptions","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Download only — don't integrate or upload","try await ensemble?.sync(options: .cloudFileRetrievalOnly)","","\/\/ Force a rebase to compact sync history","try await ensemble?.sync(options: .forceRebase)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A rebase is the most expensive part of a sync, and Ensembles decides for itself when one is due. To choose the moment yourself, sync with "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SyncOptions\/suppressRebase","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" in normal use, and when conditions suit (the device is charging, a background processing task is running) read "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/rebaseMetrics()","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and pass "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SyncOptions\/forceRebase","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" if "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/RebaseMetrics\/isRebaseRecommended","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is true or your own thresholds are met."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Process Pending Changes","anchor":"Process-Pending-Changes"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On iOS, the app may be suspended before Ensembles finishes recording a save. Call "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/processPendingChanges()","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" — for example, in a background task — to ensure all changes are fully stored:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["try await ensemble?.processPendingChanges()"]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Monitor Activity","anchor":"Monitor-Activity"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Track long-running operations via "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/currentActivity","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/activityProgress","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", or observe these notifications:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreDataEnsembleDidBeginActivity"},{"type":"text","text":" — An activity started"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreDataEnsembleDidMakeProgressWithActivity"},{"type":"text","text":" — Progress updated (includes "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SyncingPhase","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/AttachingPhase","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":")"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreDataEnsembleWillEndActivity"},{"type":"text","text":" — An activity finished (may include an error)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}]}],"references":{"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/AutoSyncPolicy":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/autosyncpolicy","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/AutoSyncPolicy","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AutoSyncPolicy"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Controls when automatic merges occur."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AutoSyncPolicy"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"AutoSyncPolicy","role":"symbol"},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/SeedPolicy/mergeAllData":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"SeedPolicy.mergeAllData","url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/seedpolicy\/mergealldata","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"mergeAllData"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SeedPolicy\/mergeAllData","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Import the local store contents and merge them with cloud data at the next merge."}]},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/SeedPolicy/excludeLocalData":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"SeedPolicy.excludeLocalData","url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/seedpolicy\/excludelocaldata","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"excludeLocalData"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SeedPolicy\/excludeLocalData","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Do not import local data. You will usually want to delete the store before attaching."}]},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles":{"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ensembles","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Sync Core Data and SwiftData stores across devices using event sourcing."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles","title":"Ensembles"},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/Syncable":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"Syncable","url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/syncable","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Syncable"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Syncable"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/Syncable","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A protocol for model types that declare how to derive a global identifier"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for Ensembles deduplication."}]},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/RebaseMetrics/isRebaseRecommended":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"isRebaseRecommended","url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/rebasemetrics\/isrebaserecommended","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"isRebaseRecommended"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":